<mxCell id="106" value="&lt;b&gt;null&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;Analyse supernatant: pH NLT 4.0 &amp;amp; turbidity (chloride) test.
a. Measure the pH of the supernatant.
b. Draw approximately 10ml of the supernatant solution into a glass tube.
c. Place 5 drops of 0.1N Silver Nitrate solution into the glass tube containing the supernatant solution.
d. Observe that no turbidity is present and the supernatant is negative for chlorides.&lt;br&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; IPC Method: pH and turbidity,&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Sample amount: 10 mL,&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Expected Result: pH NLT 4, turbidity pass,&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; IPC Failure Action: Repeat water wash with 80 L hot PW until IPC passes,&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; IPC Pass action: Continue next op,&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Estim. Time of analysis: 30 m,&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
      <mxGeometry x="220" y="6130" width="190" height="130" as="geometry"/>
